        "# Hard mode - reference to video\n\nIdentity from **reference images, video and audio** instead of a start frame.\nUp to **9 images, 3 videos, 3 soundtracks, 3 standalone audios**.\n\n## Read this first: references and keyframes are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE\n\nThis is a hard limit in ComfyUI's core, not a choice made here. `model_base.py`\nbuilds the conditioning payload like this:\n\n    if keyframes is not None:\n        payload[\"cond_video_latents\"] = [kf[\"latent\"] for kf in keyframes]\n    if refs is not None:\n        payload[\"cond_video_latents\"] = [r[\"latent\"] for r in refs ...]\n\nThe second is a plain **assignment**, so any keyframe latents are discarded\nwhile the keyframe *layout rows* survive - the sequence then desyncs and the\nsampler dies on a shape mismatch. There is no \"reference images + start frame\"\nmode, and forcing both does not degrade gracefully, it crashes.\n\nSo pick your tool per shot:\n\n| You want | Use |\n|---|---|\n| A specific opening/closing frame, or timed anchors | **H3_Keyframes.json** |\n| Identity carried by reference material | **this graph** |\n| 2-5 minute runtime | **H3_Multishot_MEMORY.json** |\n\n## Referring to your references in the prompt\n\nReference blocks are labelled in the prompt text and the numbering is\n**1-based**, while the input slots are **0-based**. So `ref_image_0` is\n`<Picture 1>`. Write prompts that name them:\n\n    <Picture 1> is the woman. <Picture 2> is the room she is standing in.\n    She walks to the window in the style of <Video 1>.\n\nOrdering is fixed by the node regardless of how you wire it: **all images, then\nvideos, then standalone audios**. A reference video WITH a soundtrack consumes\nan `<Audio j>` ordinal *before* your standalone clips - so one ref video with\nsound plus one `ref_audio_0` makes your voice clip `<Audio 2>`, not `<Audio 1>`.\n\nEmpty slots are skipped and numbering compacts, so leaving `ref_image_0` empty\nand filling `ref_image_1` still gives you `<Picture 1>`.\n\n## Reference audio must be STEREO\n\nThe audio VAE encodes `[B, 2, L]` and the layout reserves exactly two channels.\nA **mono** reference produces half the rows it reserved and dies deep in the\nmodel with no useful error. The stereo-guard node handles this - it forces\n2 channels at 32 kHz and trims length. Keep it wired.\n\n## Cost\n\nReference rows sit in the packed sequence on **every sampling step**, not just\nonce, so more references and a larger `ref_image_size` both cost time on every\nstep rather than once up front.\n\nMeasured, 124 frames at 480x864 with 2 reference images:\n\n| setting | time | identity margin |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ref_image_size = match` | 2.9 min | +9.42 |\n| `ref_image_size = max` | 4.0 min | +9.10 |\n\nSo **1.38x**, not the \"several times slower\" that core's own tooltip warns about\n- and `max` did not improve identity here, scoring fractionally worse while\ncosting 38% more. It does change the output, so it is doing something; it just\ndid not buy identity fidelity at this resolution.\n\nCaveat: that margin is a blunt measure (distance to the reference images versus\ndistance to a control person the model never saw). It confirms identity carried,\nbut may be too coarse to see the fine facial fidelity `max` targets. At higher\noutput resolutions `max` is likelier to earn its cost. Start with `match` and\n2-3 images, and reach for `max` when you can see it help.\n\nReference audio, same test: about **14%** extra wall clock, and it trims motion\nroughly 17-27% - the audio conditioning constrains the performance rather than\nstalling it.\n\n## Reference video rules\n* minimum 5 frames, or it raises\n* silently truncated to the generation length, then trimmed to `n % 17 == 5`\n* shown to the encoder at 2 fps\n\n## Before you run this\n\nThe image slots default to ComfyUI's bundled `example.png` so the graph loads\nwithout missing-file errors -- **swap in your own reference images**, they are\nthe entire point of this mode.\n\nThe reference-audio branch (LoadAudio + the stereo guard) ships **muted**,\nbecause there is no example audio to point it at. Unmute both nodes and load a\nvoice clip to use it. It is optional: identity from images alone works, and the\naudio references cost extra time on every sampling step.\n"
      ],
      "title": "HARD MODE - READ ME",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
